<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: the Listing walk reads a Thumb tbb/tbh switch table.

    Issue:      kuna GH-299 - aif plants mid-function entries; on Cortex-M
                firmware most of them sit in switch case bodies behind a
                tbb/tbh the walk could not follow.
    Stage:      P1 code/data partition - the Listing walk's computed-jump
                successors (`listing/kuna_thumbswitch.rs`).

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  The pass clears
    it and loads `thumbswitch_le32` (generator `thumbswitch_le32.py` beside it):
    a stripped Thumb ELF whose vector table makes `_start` the reset handler.
    `_start` calls 22 leaves that open with `push {r4,lr}; movs r4,#n`,
    `dispatch` at 0x8226 (`cmp r0,#3; bhi default; tbb [pc,r0]`, four cases),
    `dispatch2` at 0x8254 (`cmp r0,#3; bcs default2; tbb [pc,r0]`, three
    cases, then a zero pad byte) and `dispatch3` at 0x8274 (`cmp r0,#3; bge
    default3; tbb [pc,r0]`, three cases, then a byte that reads as an offset
    to the unreferenced `lone3` at 0x8290).  Case 1 of the first two, at
    0x8238 and 0x8264, opens with the leaves' prologue and ends in its own
    `pop {r4,pc}`.

    Before the table read, the walk stopped at every tbb and the gap walk
    listed both case bodies as sub_8238 and sub_8264.  Under `mode
    aggressive` the walk reads the first two tables, four entries behind the
    bhi and three behind the bcs, decodes the cases as the dispatchers' code,
    and lists neither.  The signed bge bounds nothing, so `dispatch3`'s table
    is not read and `lone3` stays a function.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/thumbswitch_le32</com>
  <com>mode aggressive</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>functions</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMBSWITCH #1: the bhi-guarded dispatcher is a function" min="1" max="1">0x8226 sub_8226</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMBSWITCH #2: the bhi-guarded case body is not a function" min="0" max="0">0x8238 sub_8238</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMBSWITCH #3: the bcs-guarded dispatcher is a function" min="1" max="1">0x8254 sub_8254</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMBSWITCH #4: the bcs-guarded case body is not a function" min="0" max="0">0x8264 sub_8264</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="KUNA-THUMBSWITCH #5: a bge bounds no table, so the function after it is not read as a case" min="1" max="1">0x8290 sub_8290</stringmatch>
